.TH SSH-GATE 1 "October 2026" "ssh-gate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ssh-gate \- expose SOCKS5 and HTTP proxies over one SSH tunnel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh-gate
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ssh-gate
opens a single SSH connection to a gateway host and serves local proxies over
it: SOCKS5 by default, an HTTP CONNECT proxy when asked for. Every destination
is dialed either through the tunnel or directly from the local network,
depending on the rules in
.BR DIRECT_RULES .
Hostnames routed through the tunnel are resolved with DNS-over-HTTPS queried
over the tunnel itself, so a local resolver never sees them; direct
destinations are resolved locally.
.PP
Authentication uses an Ed25519 key pair generated on first start. The public
half has to be present in the gateway's
.IR authorized_keys .
The server host key is trusted on first use and pinned in
.IR ssh_known_hosts
inside the data directory; a different key afterwards aborts every connection
attempt until that file is deleted.
.PP
Losing the SSH connection is not fatal. The proxies keep serving direct
destinations, dialing is retried with jittered backoff capped at 60 seconds,
and the readiness endpoint reports not ready until the tunnel is back up. The
process exits only on a fatal startup error, most often an invalid
configuration. Empty
.BR SSH_HOST " or " SSH_USER
is not such an error: the process keeps running with the proxies off, and only
the health endpoints and the Web UI are served until the configuration is
filled in and the service restarted.
.PP
Under systemd the tunnel state is the
.B Status:
line of
.BR "systemctl status ssh-gate" :
not configured, connecting, key not accepted by the gateway, gateway
unreachable, host key changed, other SSH error, connected or reconnecting.
A failure state names the file to act on and the time of the next attempt.
The service reports ready once its listeners are open, without waiting for the
tunnel.
.PP
A SOCKS5 client must finish its handshake within 30 seconds. A plain HTTP
proxy request is closed after 5 minutes without data in either direction;
CONNECT tunnels and SOCKS5 relays have no idle limit.
.PP
On SIGTERM or SIGINT the listeners close and running relays get 5 seconds to
finish.
.SH OPTIONS
No command-line options. All configuration is read from the environment: a
variable that is set and non-empty is used as given, otherwise the default
below applies. In the packaged form the variables live in
.IR /etc/default/ssh-gate ,
which systemd reads as an
.BR EnvironmentFile .
That file is not a shell script: only
.I KEY = value
lines, no
.BR export ,
no command substitution. Apply changes with
.BR "systemctl restart ssh-gate" .
.TP
.BI "SSH_HOST=" host
Gateway address. Required; while it is empty the proxies stay off. The tunnel
connects over IPv4 only: an IPv6 address is rejected at startup, and a name
needs an A record.
.TP
.BI "SSH_PORT=" port
Gateway SSH port. Default
.BR 22 .
.TP
.BI "SSH_USER=" user
Gateway account. Required; while it is empty the proxies stay off.
.TP
.BI "PROXY_MODES=" modes
Comma-separated list of proxies to serve:
.BR socks5 ", " http .
Default
.BR socks5 .
.TP
.BI "SOCKS5_LISTEN=" addrs
Comma-separated list of SOCKS5 listen addresses, one proxy server per
address. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1:1080 .
.TP
.BI "HTTP_LISTEN=" addrs
Comma-separated list of HTTP proxy listen addresses, one proxy server per
address. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1:3128 .
.TP
.BI "HEALTH_LISTEN=" addr
Health endpoints and web UI. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1:9090 .
.TP
.BI "UI_ALLOWED_HOSTS=" hosts
Comma-separated host names or addresses, without port, that the web UI and
the API answer to in addition to
.BR localhost ,
.BR 127.0.0.1 ,
.B ::1
and the host of
.BR HEALTH_LISTEN ,
see
.BR "HTTP INTERFACES" .
Empty by default.
.TP
.BI "MAX_CONNECTIONS=" n
Limit of concurrent client connections over all proxy listeners; a
connection over the limit is closed at once.
.B 0
disables the limit. Default
.BR 4096 .
.TP
.BI "DATA_DIR=" dir
Directory holding
.IR ssh_key ,
.IR ssh_key.pub
and
.IR ssh_known_hosts .
Default
.BR /data ;
the systemd unit sets
.BR /var/lib/ssh-gate ,
which systemd creates and owns.
.TP
.BI "DIRECT_RULES=" rules
Comma-separated destinations that bypass the tunnel, see
.BR "DIRECT RULES" .
Empty by default, which sends everything through the tunnel.
.TP
.BI "DIRECT_IP_FAMILY=" family
Address family used when dialing direct destinations:
.BR ipv4 ", " ipv6 ", " both .
Default
.BR ipv4 .
.TP
.BI "DOH_HOST=" host
DNS-over-HTTPS server for tunnel destinations, reached over HTTPS on port 443
through the tunnel. Default
.BR cloudflare-dns.com .
Empty disables DNS-over-HTTPS and leaves resolution to the local resolver.
.TP
.BI "SSH_DIAL_TIMEOUT=" dur
Deadline for dialing one destination through the tunnel. Must be positive
and under 10m, which is the size of the in-memory connection history window.
Default
.BR 30s .
.TP
.BI "SSH_KEEPALIVE_PERIOD=" dur
Idle time before keepalive probes start. Drives both the OS-level TCP
keepalive and the SSH-layer
.I keepalive@openssh.com
probe that drops a transport which is alive at TCP level but stuck.
.B 0
disables both. Default
.BR 10s .
.TP
.BI "SSH_KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL=" dur
Keepalive probe retransmission interval, rounded to whole seconds;
.B 0
keeps the kernel default of 75s. Default
.BR 1s .
.TP
.BI "SSH_KEEPALIVE_PROBES=" n
Unanswered probes before the connection is declared dead;
.B 0
keeps the kernel default of 9. Default
.BR 5 .
.PP
Worst case time to notice a dead path on the OS side is
.I period
plus
.I interval
times
.IR probes
.
With the defaults that is 15 seconds; an unanswered SSH-layer probe drops the
tunnel within about two periods.
.TP
.BI "LOG_LEVEL=" level
Level of the service log, one of
.BR debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
Default
.BR info .
.TP
.BI "ACCESS_LOG=" on|off
One line per proxied connection: client, destination, route, bytes,
duration and
.IR result :
.BR ok ", " resolve_error ", " dial_error " or " relay_error .
The error text of a failed connection is a warning in the service log with
the same
.IR conn_id .
.B LOG_LEVEL
does not affect it. Default
.BR on .
.PP
Both logs are structured JSON lines. Under systemd they go to the journal
with a syslog priority per line, the service log as
.B ssh-gate
and the access log as
.BR ssh-gate-access ;
elsewhere both go to standard error.
.SH "DIRECT RULES"
A rule names a destination that is dialed from the local network instead of
the tunnel. Three forms are accepted:
.TP
.BI ip: cidr
Matches a destination whose resolved address falls in
.IR cidr .
The address comes from the same lookup as a tunnel destination
(DNS-over-HTTPS when
.B DOH_HOST
is set), so choosing a route never shows a name to the local resolver. An
intranet name that public DNS does not know needs a
.I domain
rule instead.
.TP
.BI re: regex
Matches the destination host name against a Go regular expression. An empty
pattern is rejected rather than treated as match-all.
.TP
.I domain
Matches the name itself and any name below it, so
.I internal.local
covers
.IR db.internal.local .
.PP
Without any rule, an address literal in a private, loopback, link-local,
shared (100.64.0.0/10) or unique local range is always dialed directly. A
name routed through the tunnel whose addresses are all in these ranges is
refused: through the tunnel the gateway would dial its own local network,
for example a cloud metadata service. Add a direct rule to reach such a name
from the local network.
.PP
Host names are compared in their canonical form: case-insensitively and
without a trailing dot. The value is not shell-quoted, so one backslash in
.I DIRECT_RULES
is one backslash: write
.IR re:\e.ru$ .
.SH "HTTP INTERFACES"
All served on
.BR HEALTH_LISTEN .
The web UI and the
.B /api
endpoints have no authentication. They answer only to requests whose
.I Host
header is
.BR localhost ,
.BR 127.0.0.1 ,
.BR ::1 ,
the host of
.B HEALTH_LISTEN
or a name in
.BR UI_ALLOWED_HOSTS ,
and refuse others with 403; this blocks web pages in a local browser from
reading them through DNS rebinding. The health endpoints answer to any
.IR Host .
.TP
.B /healthz
Process is up.
.TP
.B /readyz
Tunnel is connected; answers 503 while it is down.
.TP
.B /api/status
Tunnel and configuration state as JSON.
.TP
.B /api/connections
Recent connections as JSON: the last 1000 entries within 10 minutes, kept in
memory only.
.TP
.B /
Web UI over the same data.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/bin/ssh-gate
The daemon.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/systemd/system/ssh-gate.service
Unit shipped by the package. It runs the daemon as a dynamic user with the
filesystem read-only except for the data directory.
.TP
.B /etc/default/ssh-gate
Configuration, a conffile: local edits are kept across upgrades.
.TP
.B /etc/rsyslog.d/40-ssh-gate.conf
Keeps the access log out of the syslog files when rsyslog is installed; the
journal still has it.
.TP
.B /var/lib/ssh-gate
Data directory:
.IR ssh_key ,
.IR ssh_key.pub ,
.IR ssh_known_hosts .
Kept on purge because the public half of the key pair is registered on the
gateway.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown after SIGTERM or SIGINT.
.TP
.B 78
Fatal startup error:
.B SSH_PORT
not a port, an unparsable
.BR PROXY_MODES ", " DIRECT_RULES ", " DIRECT_IP_FAMILY
or duration value, the data directory not writable, an unreadable key, or a
listen address already in use. A restart cannot fix it, so the unit lists the
status in
.B RestartPreventExitStatus
and stays failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Serve the whole LAN instead of loopback only, then restart:
.PP
.EX
sed -i 's/^SOCKS5_LISTEN=.*/SOCKS5_LISTEN=0.0.0.0:1080/' /etc/default/ssh-gate
systemctl restart ssh-gate
.EE
.PP
Route traffic through the proxy:
.PP
.EX
curl --socks5-hostname 127.0.0.1:1080 https://example.com
curl -x http://127.0.0.1:3128 https://example.com
.EE
.PP
Check whether the tunnel is up, and why not:
.PP
.EX
systemctl status ssh-gate
curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:9090/readyz
.EE
.PP
The public key to put in the gateway's
.IR authorized_keys :
.PP
.EX
cat /var/lib/ssh-gate/ssh_key.pub
.EE
.PP
Read the access log, or only the service warnings and errors:
.PP
.EX
journalctl -u ssh-gate -t ssh-gate-access -o cat
journalctl -u ssh-gate -t ssh-gate -p warning
.EE
